description:
Implement a `MicrotaskQueue` class with an `add(fn)` method. Added functions should not run immediately — they should be batched and flushed in a single `queueMicrotask` call.

**Example:**
```js
const q = new MicrotaskQueue();
const log = [];
q.add(() => log.push(1));
q.add(() => log.push(2));
// log is still [] here
await Promise.resolve();
// log is now [1, 2]
```

